request: Add a clear command that removes todos whose completed field is true. --behaviour

governor turn 1: plan -> types, commands  (There is no field called "completed" on Todo. The field that marks a todo as completed is `done`, and the `complete` command sets it, so I read the request as "remove todos where done is true". This needs a new Command variant in types. In commands it needs a clear() helper, handling in parseArgs and in run, which saves the result and reports the count.)
round 1: owners types=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 7 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 2: accept  (Oracle is green: tsc reports no errors and all 20 vitest tests pass, including the acceptance tests for clear. Those tests check that clear removes only done todos, keeps order and ids, and doesn't change its input. They also check that parseArgs recognises "clear" and that run saves the remaining todos and reports "Cleared N todo(s)" with correct pluralisation. The existing CLI transcript is unchanged, so earlier behaviour still works.)

